% TO ADD A PAPER: paste its BibTeX entry at the TOP of the matching section
% (articles / incollection / inproceedings / misc). Nothing else to edit —
% js/publications.js parses this file and renders the page.
%
% Standard fields used: author, title, journal / booktitle, volume, number,
%   pages, year, month (numeric), address, publisher, editor, series, note.
% Custom fields:
%   doi         = {10.xxxx/....}   -> rendered as a doi.org link
%   pdf         = {https://...}    -> "PDF" link (publicly accessible copy)
%   escholarship= {https://...}    -> "eScholarship" link (UC open repository)
%   openaccess  = {true}           -> paper is open access at the DOI; no
%                                     repository link is added
%   inpress     = {true}           -> accepted, not yet published
%   award       = {...}            -> shown as an award line under the entry
% If none of doi/pdf/escholarship/openaccess apply, the page automatically
% links an eScholarship search for the title (https://escholarship.org/uc/ucb).
%
% Author format: "Last, First and Last, First and ..." (diacritics welcome —
% the file is UTF-8). Given names are shown as initials on the site.
